20.5 Find the error: isotropic 6 kW transmitter, E_min = 10 mV/m (eta0 = 120 pi)
==============================================================================
  eta0/(4 pi) = 30.0000 ; eta0/(2 pi) = 60.0000
  student: r = sqrt(30 P)/E = sqrt(180000)/0.01 = 42.426 km
  correct: r = sqrt(60 P)/E = sqrt(360000) / 0.01 = 600.000/0.01 = 60.000 km ; ratio 1.41421 = sqrt 2
  brute force: E0(r) = sqrt(2 eta0 <S>) = 10 mV/m at r = 60.000000 km
  [20.5 range 60 km] OK
  at 60 km: <S> = 1.3263e-07 W/m^2 ; E0^2/(2 eta0) = 1.3263e-07
  field at 60 km if r were 42.4 km... student's E0 at 60 km would be 0.00707 V/m (= rms value 0.00707)

